IO-08: skip a UTF-8 byte order mark at the start of the input file

InputReader::read_stream() recognises a section header only when the line
starts with '['. With a UTF-8 byte order mark the first line starts with
EF BB BF, so the first section header was not seen and its lines, which
then came before any header, were dropped. The BOM is now removed from the
first line before it is looked at. Files without a BOM are read exactly as
before.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-08_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/input/InputReader.cpp b/src/engine/input/InputReader.cpp
index b74750b..018a812 100644
--- a/src/engine/input/InputReader.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/input/InputReader.cpp
@@ -118,6 +118,11 @@ bool InputReader::read_stream(std::istream& stream, SimulationContext& ctx) {
     while (std::getline(stream, raw_line)) {
         ++lines_read_;
 
+        // A UTF-8 byte order mark (files saved as "UTF-8 with BOM") is not
+        // text; left in place it hides the first section header.
+        if (lines_read_ == 1 && raw_line.compare(0, 3, "\xEF\xBB\xBF") == 0)
+            raw_line.erase(0, 3);
+
         // Strip \r (Windows CRLF)
         if (!raw_line.empty() && raw_line.back() == '\r') {
             raw_line.pop_back();
